  - {fileID: 518449342}
  - {fileID: 1050452035}
  messages:
  - Hey.\n\nToday's just training since it's your first day and all. I'll hold off
    on sending you any more orders until you've finished the one I sent already,
    so just focus on getting those done without worrying about time.\n\nJust for
    today, if you mess up an order, press the "restart order" button on the orders
    page and I'll give you another shot.\n\nMake sure to read the instructions message
    before starting your day, and good luck.
  - 'FIRST DAY INSTRUCTIONS:\n\n1. Orders will appear on this computer. Submit an
    order by placing it on the conveyor belt.\n\n2. Meat will arrive from the left
    side of the conveyor. Grab it and process it before submitting the order.\n\n3.
    Use the cutting table and bagger (if a bag is requested) to prepare meat for
    specific orders. Some machines are currently under repair and cannot be used.
    If the bagger gets clogged, press the red button to fix the issue after some
    time.\n\n4. Keep the room clean by throwing any unused meat down the trash chute.\n\nNote:
    We keep track of order errors. Employees who fail to meet our standards will
    be fired.'
  - 'Nice job finishing your first day.\n\nToday''s the real deal - so that means
    no mistakes on the orders and make sure you get them done on time.\n\nJust a
    heads up: past employees complained about something coming into the room while
    they were working.\n\nI''ll send you another message with the details. Anyway,
    that''s all for now. Keep up the good work.'
  - 'Info about the hall creature:\n\n1. The hallway lights have been unreliable
    for a while. They shut off starting from the light furthest from the door. If
    you notice that one or two are off, expect the rest to follow soon after.\n\n2.
    If you see all the lights are off, immediately turn off your room lights. Be
    aware: the switch seems to mess with the power, so you won''t be able to turn
    the lights off for a while after you do it once. This means you should only turn
    them off when absolutely necessary.\n\n3. Turning off your lights makes the creature
    think no one''s in the room, and it''ll leave you alone.\n\n4. Don''t leave the
    door open for too long. That''s a guaranteed way to let it in.'
  - 'I''ve got good news and bad news.\n\nGood news: I managed to get the cooker
    fixed overnight. To use it, toss some wood into the bottom compartment and flip
    the switch. The lower rack cooks the meat well done, while the top rack cooks
    it lightly.\n\nDon''t leave meat in there for too long though - it burns easily.\n\nBad
    news: Another monster''s active now. This one''s the reason we tell you to keep
    the room clean.\n\nI''ll send you another message with the details soon. '
  - Info about the second creature:\n\n1. This one lives down the trash chute and
    eats any meat thrown down it. If you don't feed it, it gets hungry and might
    climb up looking for food.\n\n2. You'll usually get extra meat sent down the
    conveyor. Use it to keep this thing fed and you should stay safe.\n\n3. You'll
    know to feed this thing when you start seeing small spider-like creatures around
    your room. They're harmless but they'll report the location of any food back
    to the creature when it's hungry.\n\n4. If it ever comes into the room, I suggest
    you do anything you can to throw some meat down the chute to get it to leave.
    I've also heard that it's harmless if you are looking at it, so use that to your
    advantage.
  - 'Nice job!\n\nYou''re almost through the week. I''ve got one more creature to
    send you info about. I''ll send the details shortly. '
  - 'Info about the third creature:\n\n1. Good news - this one''s harmless. It won''t
    attack you, but it will block your machines and stop you from fulfilling orders.\n\n2.
    If you find one, grab the stick I left by your desk. The creature is surprisingly
    fragile - give it a few pokes and it''ll fall apart. '
  - 'It''s the final day of the week, but that doesn''t mean you get to take any
    breaks.\n\nGood news though - last night I finally got the blender working. This
    one''s fully automatic. Just throw the meat into the chute and it''ll blend it
    into jars for you. Just a note: half pieces of meat will blend much faster since
    the larger pieces tend to clog it.'
  - Amazing job this week!\n\nNo need to clock out today, you can just go ahead and
    leave for the weekend.\n\nThanks for all your hard work.
